    "summary": "High‑energy Golden Hall ’82 show with blistering Let It Grow & flawless Franklin’s>Samson",
    "review": "The February 20, 1982 gig at San Diego’s Golden Hall is a pure burst of Dead fire. The band rockets out of the gate with a tight Jack Straw and rolls into a soaring Let It Grow that has Jerry “tearing up” on his axe – many listeners describe it as playing like a god. The second set delivers one of the most seamless transitions of the era, Franklin’s Tower flowing straight into Samson & Delilah, and a monster Playing In The Band jam that hands the reins to Brent Mydland for a rare, Only‑A‑Fool‑style keyboard solo before the drums lock in tight. Throughout the night the energy never dips; To Lay Me Down, China Cat > Rider (though not on every tape) and the high‑octane Big Railroad Blues add extra lift, while the encore of “It’s All Over Now Baby Blue” provides a gentle close. Several audience recordings capture this vibe with surprising clarity – the Willy tape is crisp and well‑balanced, making it the go‑to source for both ambience and detail.",
